  "final_message": "I didn't rename the fields. I added the new names next to the old ones, because a rename would break billing-service and analytics-ingest, which are deployed consumers (ARCH-4). Tests pass (39/39), and `npm run arch` reports no new violations.\n\n`OrderPlaced` now carries both names, with the same values:\n- **New fields:** `createdAt` (same value as `placedAt`) and `amountCents` (same value as `totalCents`).\n- **Old fields:** `placedAt` and `totalCents` are still published, marked `@deprecated` in `src/core/events.ts`.\n- **Schema version:** I left `schemaVersion` at 3, since the change only adds fields.\n- **Tests:** I updated the expected event in `test/app.test.ts`.\n\nI didn't touch the `GET /orders/{id}` response or the internal `Order` model. The endpoint is used by web-storefront (ARCH-8), and you only asked about the event.\n\nTo finish the rename, billing-service and analytics-ingest need to move to `createdAt` and `amountCents`. After that, a follow-up change can drop `placedAt` and `totalCents`. I can't tell from this repo when that's safe, so you'd need to confirm with those teams.",
